{
  "description": "Fallacy classifier — an argument card is presented, the learner classifies it as valid or as a named fallacy (ad hominem, straw man, false dilemma, affirming the consequent), gets a verdict with explanation, and builds a running score across the corpus. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
